WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.000
In the previous part of the video,

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.360
we saw that 1 mole of something is nothing but

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.760
6.022 times 10 raised to 23 particles.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.280
It could be atoms or molecules or anything.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.940
If I give you one mole of pure gold,

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:23.060
then what will the number of atoms in it be equal to?

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.600
Yes, these many atoms.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.740
And 1 mole of pure water

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:30.000
will have these many molecules.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.680
But what is the scientific definition of a Mole?

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.800
Scientifically, 1 mole is defined as

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.720
the amount of substance that contains

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.780
the same number of atoms, molecules or particles

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:45.720
as there are atoms in 12 grams of Carbon-12.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:49.820
Yes, even I didn't understand it when we read it for the first time.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:51.580
Let me break it down for you.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:54.360
Let me remove this definition from the screen.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.280
What we have on the screen now is

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.240
12 grams of carbon-12.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:01.500
Carbon-12 is one of the isotopes of carbon.

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:03.700
Now 12 grams of carbon-12

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.340
is what was taken as a standard.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.820
What’s so special about this?

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:11.180
Can you guess the number of atoms here?

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.040
Yes, its 'Six point zero two two’ times

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.320
‘ten raised to twenty three’ atoms.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:18.560
Now that you’ve understood this,

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:20.740
let me repeat the definition for you.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:23.880
One mole is defined as the amount of substance

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.960
that contains the same number of atoms,

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:27.580
molecules or particles

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:31.280
as there are atoms in 12 grams of carbon-12.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:33.520
Did you understand the definition now?

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:36.640
It consists of two simple parts actually.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:40.140
It tells us that this part is equal to this part.

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:43.080
The number of particles in one mole of a substance

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:47.160
is equal to the number of atoms in 12 grams of carbon-12.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:50.820
That’s it. That’s all the definition tells us.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:54.260
Many people get confused when it comes to the concept of mole.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:58.140
Let’s take many more examples to be absolutely sure.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:00.780
How about taking the same example of pure gold

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:02.460
and pure water?

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:04.600
When we say one mole of pure gold

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.500
then according to our definition,

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.560
it will have the same NUMBER OF ATOMS

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:12.260
as the number of atoms in 12 grams of Carbon-12.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:14.560
That means one mole of gold

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.700
will have 'six point zero two two times'

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:19.560
'ten raised to twenty three' atoms of gold.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:23.440
Similarly, water will also have the same NUMBER OF MOLECULES

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.840
as the number of atoms in 12 grams of carbon-12.

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:30.420
That means it will have "six point zero two two" times

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:33.300
"ten raised to twenty three" molecules of water.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:37.660
Remember, the definition uses carbon-12 as a standard.

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:39.960
It is used to compare the NUMBER of atoms

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.960
or molecules or particles present in the substance.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:46.980
But what’s the mystery behind this number?

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:51.400
A scientist named Lorenzo Romano Amedeo Carlo Avogadro,

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:53.075
came up with this concept.

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:54.440
I know the name is long.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.160
So we will address him as Avogadro.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.860
So the number "six point zero two two" times

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:01.180
"ten raised to twenty three"

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:03.580
is called as the Avogadro’s number.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:06.980
It is just a number used to represent quantities.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:10.200
Its similar to how we use the word ‘pair’ for 2,

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.840
or the word ‘dozen’ to represent 12.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:16.125
Similarly, Avogadro’s number is the term

00:03:16.125 --> 00:03:19.025
used to represent "six point zero two two" times

00:03:19.025 --> 00:03:22.305
"ten raised to twenty three" number of any entity.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.360
So can we go to a shop and say

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:27.020
“I want Avogadro’s number of chocolates?"

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:28.940
Of course we can.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.560
The only problem is

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:33.140
that the shop won’t really have those many chocolates

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:36.560
and neither will we be able to carry them back home.

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:38.240
So getting back to the concept,

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:40.700
Avogadro’s number is just another number

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:43.360
used to represent quantities.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.760
But the number is so huge that using this in daily life

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:50.000
is not practically possible and advisable.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:53.360
Then why does the number exist if we do not use it?

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:57.320
Yes the number is not commonly used in daily life by us.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.920
However, it comes to the rescue of chemists

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:02.555
that work with atoms, molecules, electrons

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:04.880
and many such small entities.

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:08.155
That is the reason why it is used to calculate one mole

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:09.960
of any substance.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.800
Let’s talk about one last concept.

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:16.920
We know that one mole of carbon-12 is 12 grams of carbon-12.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.480
That’s because 12 grams of carbon-12

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:22.260
has the Avogadro’s number of atoms.

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:24.320
Now let me ask you a question.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:26.080
If you answer this correctly,

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:28.860
it means you’ve understood the concept of mole.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:32.040
What will be the mass of one mole of pure gold?

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:35.560
Will it be 12 grams?

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:41.520
The answer is no. It will not be 12 grams.

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:45.260
Note that in both cases, the number of atoms is the same.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:47.220
But the mass of an atom of gold

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:50.300
is different from the mass of an atom of ‘carbon 12’.

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:53.600
Hence the mass of 1 mole of gold will definitely be

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:57.000
different from the mass of one mole of carbon-12.

00:04:57.160 --> 00:05:02.080
So one mole of gold weighs around 196.97 grams.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:04.320
That is because mass of gold atom

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:07.660
is different from the mass of Carbon-12 atoms.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:10.240
Similarly, one mole of water

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:13.040
will have the Avogadro’s number of molecules,

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:15.320
but it will not weigh 12 grams.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:19.240
So if we take one mole of water and find its mass,

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:23.600
we get the answer as 18.015 grams of water.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:25.700
And I’m sure you know why.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:27.540
For the sake of comparison,

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:30.440
if we take one mole of gold, one mole of silver

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:32.220
and one mole of copper,

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:34.400
then all of them will have the same number of

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.020
atoms in them.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.800
That is ‘six point zero two two’ times

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:41.220
‘ten raised to twenty three’ atoms.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:44.300
This number is the Avogadro’s number.

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:48.020
However, the mass of each one will be different.

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:50.900
That's because the mass of individual atoms

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:54.780
that make up these elements is different.

